<title>USA: CME Nov lumber falls the limit on weak cash tone.</title>
<headline>CME Nov lumber falls the limit on weak cash tone.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A soft tone in the cash lumber market pushed the CME November contract down the daily $10.00 per thousand board feet trading limit, but bargain hunting quickly moved the contract off limit, trade sources said.</p>
<p>At 0921 CST, November lumber was down $9.80 per tbf at $402.40, with other contracts down $0.60 to $7.40 per tbf.</p>
<p>--Anna Driver 312-983-7294.</p>
